@end multitable

@section Building the Bacon Module

The @command{cmacsgi} module is compiled into the CMacs binary by
default (via the bundled libbacon static link).  For standalone or
development use, it can also be built as a loadable @file{.so}:

@example
cd cmacs/bacon/modules/
make
@end example

This produces @file{cmacs_gi.so} for use with an external
@command{bacon} binary.

@section Compile Flags

The Emacs build system picks up CMacs objects via @code{configure.ac}:

@example
CMACS_GLIB_OBJ="cmacs-glib-loop.o cmacs-gobject.o
                 cmacs-gclosure.o cmacs-dbus-service.o
                 cmacs-eval-dispatch.o"
CMACS_GI_OBJ="cmacs-gi.o"
CMACS_CRISPY_OBJ="cmacs-crispy.o"
CMACS_BACON_OBJ="cmacs-bacon.o cmacs-bacon-ipc.o"
@end example

C source files live under @file{cmacs/} and are symlinked into
@file{src/} for the build system.

@bye
